DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ppppppxx and ppppppaacc drivers works with the npppd(8) daemon to provide net‐
     work interfaces for Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) sessions by request
     from the daemon.  ppppppxx operates by allocating a network interface for
     each PPP session.  ppppppaacc concentrates multiple PPP sessions on a single
     network interface.  The interfaces also work with pipex(4) to accelerate
     the performance of data packet forwarding, and supports ioctls which are
     added by pipex(4).

     To use ppppppxx or ppppppaacc from npppd(8) the administrator needs to configure
     the interface configuration in npppd.conf(5).  Also the administrator
     needs to enable pipex(4) by setting _n_e_t_._p_i_p_e_x_._e_n_a_b_l_e to ‘1’ using
     sysctl(8).

